WEBVTT

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.970
The year After Colony 195.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.980
A group of Colony citizens
hostile toward the Alliance…

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.890
…sent young men to Earth
on five Gundams.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.060
The project name was
Operation Meteor.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.330
At the end of an involved battle…

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.120
…the sole revolutionary leader,
Treize Khushrenada…

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.580
…took on the task of closing
the curtain on an era…

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.160
…and died in battle.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.960
That gave way to the birth…

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.580
…of the Earth Sphere
Unified Nation.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.050
After Colony 196.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.170
No military weapons remain
in the Earth Sphere.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:06.020
However, as long as
mankind exists…

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.480
…there will always be battles.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:18.490
<i>Gundam Wing</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:18.490
<i></i>Special Edition

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:18.490
<i></i>Special Edition

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.190
This is Water.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.900
I’ve confirmed our target.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.790
I’ve locked on.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.040
Neo-titanium?

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.210
How did this get here?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.990
As long as peace continues,
there’s no need for Gundams.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.740
It’s tough parting with them.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.780
No, it’s okay.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.490
Let’s hurry and send them
into the sun…

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.440
…with this disposal block.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.610
Right.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.430
Good-bye, my Sandrock.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.360
See ya later, old pal.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:44.360
Wufei didn’t bring
his after all.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:45.620
No, he didn’t.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.320
Heero and Trowa sent their
Gundams to me right away.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.660
I wonder how everyone’s doing.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.340
At the natural resources
satellite MO-II…

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.760
…a ceremony was being held…

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.500
…to mark the first anniversary
of the war’s end.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.260
One year ago…

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.640
…people didn’t have the peace
of mind to enjoy Christmas.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.480
Things have sure changed.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.930
We are here to remember
the many lives lost…

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.230
…as a result of a foolish war.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.810
However, those lives were
not lost in vain.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.660
That’s because the many
departed souls…

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.740
…left us with valuable lessons
and tools for reflection.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.080
So finally, we’ve been
able to attain peace.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.880
Those many precious lives have
become the foundation…

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.870
The president doesn’t get it.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:47.000
It’s harder to maintain peace
than it is to attain it.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.630
He understands that.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.260
Otherwise, the government…

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.600
…wouldn’t financially back
us “Preventers”.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.220
He’s pretty smart for a person
elected democratically.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:01.560
Sure you can miss the
rest of the ceremony?

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.440
<i>Preventers only put
out fires.</i>

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.980
<i>These ceremonies don’t suit us.</i>

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:07.950
<i>So?</i>

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.660
There’s a possibility that
the Neo-titanium…

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.660
…is from the thirteenth
constellation.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.240
<i>You mean it’s a new
mobile suit model?</i>

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.250
I’m using various sources…

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.410
…to determine where it’s from.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.450
We’ve gotta put out this fire
while it’s still small.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.920
<i>This isn’t going to
be quite as simple…</i>

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.710
<i>…as our last few missions.</i>

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.380
I agree.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.860
As you’re aware…

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.850
…it’s been only seven years…

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:48.520
…since Colony L3 X-18999
was completed.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.410
We’ve invited people from Earth
to come live here…

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.870
…but our unstable economy…

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.990
…is preventing the population
from growing.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.420
The problem is whether
the citizens understand…

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:02.170
…that they’re members of the
Earth Sphere Unified Nation.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.130
One can’t expect a stable
lifestyle…

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.130
…if one’s own colony alone
is prospering.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.630
But we’ve been told
that many citizens here…

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.180
…hope for a strong leader
to rise up and guide them.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.550
Someone like yourself,
Vice Foreign Minister Darlian.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.860
That’s a shame.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:30.980
Finally, true peace and
freedom has been attained…

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.150
…and yet…

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.500
Be gentle with her.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.960
Understood, sir.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.790
Our scheme is complete now.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.340
That’s right.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:55.810
Those lacking leadership
should make way…

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.560
…for those possessing it.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:02.430
<i>It is our sincere wish that
peace will last forever.</i>

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.030
Nothing wrong with
wishing for peace.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.780
The real question is whether
mankind is ready for it.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.160
We’ll just have to teach
them how to deal with it.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.370
Right, Dekim?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.250
Correct, Miss Mariemaia.

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:24.170
My father entrusted me with
these Christmas presents.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.490
I must deliver them to
the people.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:39.670
I can’t believe how small
the crowd is today.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:46.510
It looks like this colony has
other forms of entertainment.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.850
Other forms of entertainment?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.190
What do you mean?

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:53.160
I’m gonna check it out.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:56.150
Trowa?

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.860
Trowa…

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.210
The Barton Foundation?

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.140
I guess he hasn’t given up yet.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:20.420
Or maybe it’s Leia’s daughter.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.880
I think her name was Mariemaia.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:34.520
Hey, No-Name…

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.900
I’ll show you something
I’ve never shown anyone.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:43.910
Her name is Mariemaia;
she’s my sister’s daughter.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.460
She’ll be Earth’s leader
after we conquer it.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.130
Mariemaia Barton.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:09.220
Born in After Colony 189.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:12.280
Deceased two years
after her birth.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.740
Father: Unknown.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.860
It’s Christmas.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.370
But someone always
gets stuck working.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.870
Didn’t know Trowa had a niece.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.450
So the records say.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.620
But the Trowa we know
isn’t the real Trowa Barton.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.380
Right, I almost forgot.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.380
You going?

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.500
Yeah.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.500
Relena’s been kidnapped.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.850
Anything for the one you love.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.800
Comrades.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.300
The time has come to stand up
for Miss Mariemaia.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.770
We thank you all
for your efforts…

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.940
…to tolerate the
intolerable…

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.360
…and bear the unbearable
over this past year.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.810
Today you are starting
on the road to glory!

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:01.740
The awakening of a new
humanity…

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.660
…will be triggered by
the soldiers of Mariemaia…

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.910
…and we shall be the symbol
of hope for the people.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.290
But first…

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.990
…we must eliminate
all threatening elements.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.620
Trowa Barton, to the front!

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.550
Hold it.

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.680
Wufei.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.780
<i>This is Water.</i>

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.740
<i>Respond on secret lines
D to R.</i>

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.910
This is Fire.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.820
Line is secured; go ahead.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.830
<i>I found out where
the fire started.</i>

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.820
Is it L3?

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.830
<i>Your instincts still amaze me.</i>

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.380
It wasn’t hard to figure out,
considering the areas searched.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.920
Did you determine which
colony it is?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.420
<i>The new colony, X-18999.</i>

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.210
Who’s the leader?

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:04.300
<i>Mariemaia Barton.</i>

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:05.880
Barton?

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.520
<i>As I feared, we’re too late.</i>

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.230
<i>I expect they’ll declare
independence or war…</i>

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.110
<i>…against Earth within
a few hours.</i>

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.070
<i>And the bad news
doesn’t end there.</i>

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.070
What else?

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>Vice Foreign Minister Darlian
has been missing…</i>

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.440
<i>…since her last official
visit to X-18999.</i>

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:25.370
Relena?!

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.160
<i>I think we’d better hurry.</i>

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.570
Roger.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:30.910
We’ll change our rendezvous
point.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.480
So, you’re awake.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.550
Who are you?

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.770
Have you been kidnapped too?

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:58.780
No.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.400
I’m the one that ordered
you brought here.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.230
What are you talking about?

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:08.110
My name is Mariemaia
Khushrenada.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.330
Daughter of Treize
Khushrenada.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.820
You’re joking.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:13.920
It’s no joke.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.460
It’s been proven through
DNA testing.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:17.250
But…

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:20.120
I hear there’s a so-called
adult world…

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.300
…that kids don’t understand.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.380
So I can’t begin to explain…

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.840
…how I’ve come to live
in this world.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:29.220
But the facts are the facts.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.640
And I intend to carry
out my father’s wishes.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.690
I don’t know who’s been
telling you these stories.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.190
But you’re mistaken.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.350
Enough!

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.480
That’s enough.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.980
I’ve been chosen to lead
the Earth Sphere Unified Nation.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:45.190
I won’t allow such rude talk!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:50.870
It’s nothing.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.910
Leave the room.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.030
Ma’am!

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.330
This room is under surveillance.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.790
So don’t try anything funny.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.090
I am meeting you like this
out of respect…

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.170
…for the fact that you
were once Queen Relena.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.930
Be more careful in the future.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.640
Let me ask you this.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:17.020
What do you plan to do
with me now?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.680
You’ll find out soon enough.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.740
What do you plan on doing?

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:46.790
<i>I’m supposed to be going
to X-18999 with Heero.</i>

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:51.010
<i>I’m sure we’re gonna have
a blast of a party there.</i>

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.770
Without the Gundams?

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.730
Have you forgotten we don’t
have our Gundams anymore?!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.510
<i>Heero says that really
makes no difference.</i>

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:00.720
B-But still…

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.890
<i>Don’t worry!</i>

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:05.530
<i>We don’t even know
who the enemy is yet.</i>

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.730
<i>And there might not even
be a need for our Gundams.</i>

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.370
Even if it does become
a mobile suit battle…

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.280
…we could steal a couple
of their suits and fight back.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:23.590
If you leave him alone…

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.880
…Quatre always takes the blame
himself for everything.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.260
One day he’ll say that
his lack of effort…

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.500
…is the reason there’s no air
in outer space.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:43.230
We’re faced with great danger
and I’ve taken the only means

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.570
…to counter this situation…

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.560
Duo, I’m going out to
get our Gundams back.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:50.770
<i>What?!</i>

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:53.450
<i>But we’ve already disposed
of them into the sun!</i>

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:56.290
If I left now, I’d still be able
to get them in time.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:00.070
<i>Okay.</i>

00:15:00.070 --> 00:15:01.120
<i>Good luck!</i>

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.550
It’s going to be impossible
to communicate in real time…

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.010
…so let’s contact each other
regularly by mail.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:08.880
<i>Roger.</i>

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.220
<i>Have a safe trip.</i>

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.040
That goes for you, too.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:24.650
Are we done?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.480
The docking is complete.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.730
But the direction controls
are extremely delicate.

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.640
You pilot the spacecraft.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.160
Yeah, no problem.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:41.160
I’m grateful to have you
guys accompany me, Rashid.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.820
Don’t mention it, Master Quatre.

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:46.410
It’s all my fault to begin with.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:50.050
If I hadn’t mentioned sending
the Gundams into the sun…

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.840
…this wouldn’t have happened.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.890
No one could have predicted
this would happen.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:58.500
Let’s just concentrate on
the immediate problem.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.480
Yes, you’re right.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.270
Do you think we can still
catch up…

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.100
…to the Gundam disposal block?

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:09.850
The block is over fifty days
away from Venus’ orbit.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.700
With this Interplanetary
Transport Ship…

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.070
…we should barely
catch up to it.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.740
Don’t worry, everything
will work out fine.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.240
We wouldn’t want to return
to find the Earth gone.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.530
It all depends on us.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.730
I’m back to being
the God of Death.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:16.580
So long… buddy.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.600
What happened?!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.510
Why won’t it explode?!

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:25.390
What did I do wrong?!

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.550
Duo!

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:32.350
Deathscythe is a superb
piece of art!

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:35.190
Think of a better way,
rather than destroying it.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:40.320
I won’t let my buddy be
used for mass destruction!

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.040
So you were planning
to kill me…

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.080
…after you destroyed
Deathscythe.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.880
I was gonna kill everyone here.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.620
Including myself.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.300
If it meant peace
for this colony…

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.470
…I’d be the God of Death
any day.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.920
If you’d go that far,
then try and outwit me.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:17:59.890
What?

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.350
Duo, steal Deathscythe!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:03.510
Huh?!

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:05.730
Forget Operation Meteor!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.930
Take it to the Earth now.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.150
There’s a man called Howard
on the Pacific Ocean.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.980
You can rely on him.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.690
Of course, go as
the God of Death.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.450
The God of Death.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.820
It’s a lot better than being
the hero of a massacre.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:29.790
We went to all that trouble
just to obtain peace.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.990
Now someone’s gotta help
maintain it, right?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.250
Heero?

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:38.930
If you wanted to sleep,
why didn’t you say so?

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.190
<i>Are you lost?</i>

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.910
<i>I said, are you lost?</i>

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:13.790
<i>I’ve been lost ever since
I was born.</i>

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.200
<i>Oh, that’s so sad.</i>

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.340
<i>Well, I’m not lost.</i>

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.290
<i>I’m taking Mary out for a walk.</i>

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.510
<i>Here.</i>

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.510
<i>I’ll give you this flower.</i>

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:33.150
<i>Wait for me, Mary!</i>

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.720
<i>Mary!</i>

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:52.080
<i>Mission complete.</i>

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.690
<i>That’s ludicrous!</i>

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:16.120
<i>You mean use the Gundam
as a tool of carnage?!</i>

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.160
<i>This is a war!</i>

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.960
<i>Sacrificing the general
public is of no relevance.</i>

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:21.920
<i>Got it?</i>

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.250
<i>Now retrain him at once!</i>

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:29.930
<i>Our weapon has no use
for human kindness!</i>

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:31.260
<i>You’re right.</i>

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.980
<i>But do you really believe…</i>

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:37.520
<i>…Heero Yuy would be pleased
if we obliterated mankind?</i>

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:41.980
<i>Heero! Hey, Heero!</i>

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.230
Wake up!

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:46.650
What is it?

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:49.900
The little girl is about
to issue a statement.

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:54.830
<i>We, at Colony L3 X-18999
hereby wish to announce…</i>

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:58.870
<i>…our independence from the
Earth Sphere Unified Nation…</i>

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:00.420
<i>…and declare war!</i>

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:04.460
<i>I am a legitimate heir
of the World Nation Sovereign.</i>

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:08.510
<i>My name is Mariemaia
Khushrenada…</i>

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:11.040
<i>…daughter of Treize Khushrenada.</i>

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:12.010
What?!

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:13.350
Treize’s daughter?!

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:15.600
<i>I’m carrying out my
father’s will.</i>

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:19.810
<i>It’s in human nature to fight!</i>

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:23.570
How could this happen?!

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:25.740
Why couldn’t you have
prevented this?!

00:22:26.310 --> 00:22:29.110
I reported this matter
the other day.

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:30.820
<i>I know that!</i>

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:34.280
<i>But your department
receives sufficient funds…</i>

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:35.450
<i>…to prevent these situations!</i>

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:37.580
I understand that.

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:41.000
We’re doing everything to
stop this from progressing.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.170
But it seems they’d
prepared for this…

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:47.540
…even before our department
was ever formed.

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:54.430
I can stand here and
make excuses all day.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:56.430
But the question remains…

00:22:57.090 --> 00:23:00.900
…whether or not we can stop
their aggression without help.

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:02.480
Who’re you?

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:03.760
Excuse me.

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:05.230
You’re…

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:08.060
I’ve come to ask for
a code name.

00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:10.570
I’d like the name Wind…

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.650
…appropriate for one who
puts out fires.

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:19.120
We’re almost in the L3 Area.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.410
So how do you suggest
we get in?

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.790
We could take over
a couple mobile suits.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:27.210
But we’d probably be
targeted while boarding.

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.050
Then we’ll have to fly
straight through.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.920
It’s the only way.

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.170
Man!

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:35.810
How about using your head?

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:36.720
You too.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:37.350
What?!

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:39.770
Unidentified shuttle ahead!

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:42.300
It’s flying into the
troop of mobile suits!

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.310
Attention, approaching shuttle!

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:46.150
This is a danger zone!

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:47.150
Retreat!

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:48.780
<i>Yo! Long time no see!</i>

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:50.100
Duo…

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:51.480
And Heero?!

00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:54.660
<i>Seems they’re gonna have
quite a Christmas party.</i>

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:56.950
<i>Thought we’d give them
a little present.</i>

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:59.200
Not without your Gundams!

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:01.000
You have no way to retaliate!

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:03.080
<i>I’m sure we’ll think
of something.</i>

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.700
<i>That’s if we can get
to the colony.</i>

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:07.090
Duo, Heero.

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.670
Why don’t you join
forces with us once more?

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:12.130
<i>I’ll think about it when
the time comes.</i>

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:13.630
<i>See ya!</i>

00:24:13.630 --> 00:24:16.300
<i>We don’t want to be late
for the party!</i>

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:17.300
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:20.310
<i>Don’t blame us if they
run out of food.</i>

00:24:20.670 --> 00:24:22.390
They haven’t changed.

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:25.100
Sally, we’ll have to contain the
Tauruses ourselves.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.360
Let’s divert their attention
to us.

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:28.320
Okay!

00:24:28.320 --> 00:24:30.650
So we’re backing them up,
after all.

00:24:30.650 --> 00:24:33.320
But right now, we’ve gotta
depend on them.

00:24:33.320 --> 00:24:34.360
Yes.

00:24:34.360 --> 00:24:36.070
That’s what’s so reassuring!

00:24:42.360 --> 00:24:45.210
How’s this for some
shuttle maneuvering?!

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:48.290
I was counting on those skills
right from the beginning.

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:49.910
That’s good to hear!

00:25:38.330 --> 00:25:39.720
Hold on tight!

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:41.510
We’re going in!

00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:49.810
Outta my way!

00:26:22.130 --> 00:26:24.850
I’m surprised they kept this
many mobile suits intact!

00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:41.620
Staying here will only work
to our disadvantage!

00:26:41.620 --> 00:26:43.830
<i>Destroy all you can,
then escape.</i>

00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:46.610
<i>Proceed at your own discretion.</i>

00:26:46.610 --> 00:26:47.400
Roger!

00:26:53.530 --> 00:26:55.500
It’s a new model!

00:27:01.500 --> 00:27:03.590
He’s pretty good.

00:27:06.130 --> 00:27:07.640
Hey, I know this…

00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:09.590
I know this style of combat!

00:27:16.470 --> 00:27:17.690
No question!

00:27:17.690 --> 00:27:19.400
Trowa’s in that suit!

00:27:19.400 --> 00:27:20.900
Take this!

00:27:20.900 --> 00:27:22.270
Damn it!

00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:47.640
I’ve always wanted
to fight you like this!

00:27:55.510 --> 00:27:57.480
What’s going on, Wufei?!

00:27:57.480 --> 00:27:59.320
Are you guys doing
the right thing?

00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:00.440
What?!

00:28:05.610 --> 00:28:08.440
I’m asking if you guys
are doing the right thing!!

00:28:14.280 --> 00:28:15.290
Wufei!

00:28:15.290 --> 00:28:17.330
Hit the self-detonation switch!

00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:33.560
I repeat…

00:28:33.560 --> 00:28:34.600
Hit the switch.

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:45.780
T-Trowa.

00:28:45.780 --> 00:28:47.030
Why have you betrayed us?!

00:28:48.110 --> 00:28:49.370
Got the wrong guy.

00:28:49.370 --> 00:28:50.740
I’m not Trowa.

00:28:52.570 --> 00:28:54.360
You’re not serious!?

00:29:00.700 --> 00:29:02.660
So this’ll end everything?!

00:29:19.720 --> 00:29:21.930
I am not Trowa.

00:29:21.930 --> 00:29:24.570
I’m a nameless soldier
who’s been on the battlefield…

00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:26.030
…for as long as I remember.

00:29:32.610 --> 00:29:35.500
The first time I met
the man called Trowa…

00:29:35.500 --> 00:29:37.670
…I was helping with
adjustments to Heavyarms.

00:29:38.660 --> 00:29:40.170
What’s this all about?

00:29:40.170 --> 00:29:43.120
Why are we limiting all
our attacks to OZ?!

00:29:43.120 --> 00:29:45.340
If we proceeded with
Operation Meteor…

00:29:45.340 --> 00:29:47.550
…two billion people will die.

00:29:47.550 --> 00:29:50.600
Don’t you think this is going
too far for revenge…

00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:52.010
…for Heero Yuy, Trowa?

00:29:52.010 --> 00:29:54.680
The purpose of this plan
is not revenge!

00:29:54.680 --> 00:29:56.890
The plan is for the colonies
to conquer Earth…

00:29:56.890 --> 00:29:59.900
…for the awakening
of a “new mankind”!

00:30:00.510 --> 00:30:02.650
That sounds like something…

00:30:02.650 --> 00:30:05.030
…Dekim of the Barton
Foundation would dream up.

00:30:05.030 --> 00:30:06.030
I see.

00:30:06.030 --> 00:30:08.660
You guys have something
against that?

00:30:08.660 --> 00:30:12.450
You’re jealous that my father
and the Barton Foundation…

00:30:12.690 --> 00:30:14.160
…will rule the Earth Sphere.

00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:15.410
Where are you going, Trowa?!

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:18.000
To tell this to my father.

00:30:19.960 --> 00:30:21.420
Just watch me.

00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:25.580
I’ll proceed with Operation
Meteor by myself, if I must.

00:30:30.330 --> 00:30:32.210
Now you’ve done it.

00:30:32.210 --> 00:30:33.470
I’m sorry.

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:35.800
But I have family on Earth…

00:30:37.550 --> 00:30:38.890
Who’s there?!

00:30:39.720 --> 00:30:41.360
I have no name.

00:30:41.360 --> 00:30:43.440
If you like, call me “No-Name”.

00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:45.400
You saw us?!

00:30:46.020 --> 00:30:48.530
I’ll understand if you
want to kill me.

00:30:48.530 --> 00:30:50.560
But I might retaliate.

00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:51.570
Don’t.

00:30:51.570 --> 00:30:54.330
They’ll find out about
this sooner or later.

00:30:54.330 --> 00:30:57.610
There’s no use trying
to hide the facts.

00:30:57.610 --> 00:30:59.250
You’re giving up too easily.

00:30:59.250 --> 00:30:59.830
What?

00:31:00.700 --> 00:31:03.660
I was feeling insecure
without a name.

00:31:03.660 --> 00:31:05.960
I wouldn’t mind taking
on his name.

00:31:06.790 --> 00:31:08.550
What are you talking about?

00:31:08.550 --> 00:31:11.340
I seem to be best suited
for the battlefields.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:15.310
Are you saying you’ll pilot
this suit, Heavyarms?

00:31:15.880 --> 00:31:17.920
I like this suit.

00:31:18.260 --> 00:31:20.890
But I have no interest
in conquering Earth.

00:31:24.050 --> 00:31:25.560
All right.

00:31:25.560 --> 00:31:28.610
As of this moment, your
name is Trowa Barton.

00:31:28.610 --> 00:31:31.270
You are now in charge
of Operation Meteor!

00:31:33.310 --> 00:31:34.610
I understand.

00:32:06.760 --> 00:32:07.930
Trowa…

00:32:11.980 --> 00:32:14.940
Couldn’t he have taken things
a little easier?

00:32:23.950 --> 00:32:27.920
At this rate, it’ll take us
five more days to rendezvous…

00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:29.800
…with the resources disposal
satellite.

00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:32.830
We could reduce the time…

00:32:32.830 --> 00:32:35.340
…by up to eighty hours
on this route.

00:32:35.340 --> 00:32:38.420
Then, let’s take that route!

00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:41.560
But considering the fuel
needed to accelerate now…

00:32:41.560 --> 00:32:43.690
…and decelerate at the
rendezvous point…

00:32:43.690 --> 00:32:46.980
…we’d have no propulsion
by the time we got there.

00:32:46.980 --> 00:32:49.720
Then there’s no way
to get back?

00:32:49.720 --> 00:32:52.150
No, there’s a way to get back.

00:32:52.150 --> 00:32:54.820
If we detonated the power
generator…

00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:56.820
…and used the explosion
as our propulsion…

00:32:56.820 --> 00:32:58.780
…we could return to Earth
in no time.

00:32:59.360 --> 00:33:01.200
We’d fly the ship to Venus…

00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:04.490
…and use the catapult effect
of its gravity to get to Earth.

00:33:04.490 --> 00:33:07.580
Our main problem is the time
we have at the rendezvous point.

00:33:07.580 --> 00:33:09.200
According to calculations…

00:33:09.200 --> 00:33:12.790
…this ship’ll run alongside the
satellite for only five seconds!

00:33:12.790 --> 00:33:16.050
How many people can we
get on in five seconds?

00:33:16.050 --> 00:33:18.750
<i>Some</i> danger can’t be avoided.

00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:21.350
Since Duo’s scheduled message
hasn’t arrived…

00:33:21.350 --> 00:33:24.630
…it’s likely that things are
getting more difficult there.

00:33:24.630 --> 00:33:26.510
Then it’s decided.

00:33:26.510 --> 00:33:29.560
Our satellite team will consist
of Abdul, myself, and…

00:33:29.560 --> 00:33:32.030
No, I’ll be going alone.

00:33:32.030 --> 00:33:33.070
Master Quatre!

00:33:33.070 --> 00:33:35.860
Please, take us with you!

00:33:36.480 --> 00:33:39.320
Rashid, start the booster
one last time.

00:33:39.900 --> 00:33:44.910
Each of us is ready to give
up his life for you, anytime!

00:33:47.910 --> 00:33:51.250
In this universe, nothing is
more precious than life.

00:33:51.250 --> 00:33:54.080
Sandrock made that clear to me.

00:34:05.510 --> 00:34:08.300
The Taurus troops ahead…

00:34:08.300 --> 00:34:10.690
…are heading toward
the relay station.

00:34:10.690 --> 00:34:12.610
They’re taking a roundabout
route.

00:34:12.610 --> 00:34:14.810
But their destination
is still Earth.

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:18.940
A Preventer cruiser will arrive
from the Lunar Base shortly.

00:34:18.940 --> 00:34:22.270
I’m sure we can buy some
time when they arrive.

00:34:22.270 --> 00:34:24.400
Any word from Heero
and Duo?

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:27.490
Really…

00:34:27.820 --> 00:34:28.750
Sally.

00:34:28.750 --> 00:34:32.120
Did you confirm any new suit
models in the last battle?

00:34:32.120 --> 00:34:33.000
No.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:36.410
Come to think of it, they were
all Taurus and Space Leos.

00:34:36.790 --> 00:34:38.050
We’ve underestimated them.

00:34:38.750 --> 00:34:40.140
Just as I thought.

00:34:40.140 --> 00:34:42.140
The heat detector shows nothing.

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:44.970
So those troops consisted
primarily of mobile dolls!

00:34:44.970 --> 00:34:45.930
Right.

00:34:45.930 --> 00:34:48.810
That means the main troops
with the new mobile suits…

00:34:48.810 --> 00:34:50.190
…are deployed elsewhere.

00:34:50.190 --> 00:34:51.980
Quite an elaborate operation.

00:34:51.980 --> 00:34:54.070
Then where could the
main troops be?

00:34:54.070 --> 00:34:56.360
In any case, we’ll leave this area!

00:34:56.360 --> 00:34:58.110
Contact Earth at once!

00:34:58.110 --> 00:34:59.490
Roger!

00:35:17.580 --> 00:35:21.670
These people have no idea
what Mariemaia will do to them.

00:35:26.380 --> 00:35:29.980
But with the world’s lack
of strength to retaliate…

00:35:29.980 --> 00:35:32.400
…she won’t need five minutes
to take political control.

00:35:33.010 --> 00:35:36.810
What would you do in
this situation, Treize?

00:35:39.100 --> 00:35:41.600
We found the resources
disposal satellite.

00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:45.030
We’ve got about three hours
before we reach the satellite.

00:35:45.030 --> 00:35:47.650
I’m almost there, Sandrock.

00:35:48.570 --> 00:35:50.160
Self-detonation device?

00:35:50.160 --> 00:35:51.120
That’s right.

00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:53.250
It’s been installed in Sandrock.

00:35:53.250 --> 00:35:55.120
For confidentiality?

00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:56.880
No, that’s not why.

00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:59.510
It’s because those with power
must be prepared…

00:35:59.510 --> 00:36:01.410
…to lose their lives.

00:36:01.410 --> 00:36:03.500
I don’t quite understand.

00:36:03.500 --> 00:36:04.960
I guess not.

00:36:05.340 --> 00:36:07.260
You don’t need to understand
just yet.

00:36:08.300 --> 00:36:10.100
An order from the organization?

00:36:10.100 --> 00:36:10.980
Yeah.

00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:13.010
But forget this thing!

00:36:14.550 --> 00:36:15.610
Quatre.

00:36:15.610 --> 00:36:17.820
Fight as your heart tells you.

00:36:19.140 --> 00:36:22.070
And use the self-detonation
device…

00:36:22.070 --> 00:36:24.110
…only when you feel
you must.

00:36:24.690 --> 00:36:25.860
Yes.

00:36:33.740 --> 00:36:37.620
I can’t take away his
kindness and purity.

00:36:38.410 --> 00:36:42.590
Although this may end up being
a crueler destiny for him…

00:36:42.590 --> 00:36:44.750
…than Operation Meteor.

00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:03.070
My calculations are accurate.

00:37:03.070 --> 00:37:05.110
Unlike those of Quinze.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:16.920
So what if you rule
the Earth Sphere?

00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:19.380
Are you sure you’d be
carrying on Treize’s…

00:37:19.380 --> 00:37:22.130
…I mean, your father’s will
by doing this?

00:37:22.130 --> 00:37:23.840
You’ve got it wrong.

00:37:23.840 --> 00:37:26.250
I just want to be victorious.

00:37:26.250 --> 00:37:28.180
Then you’ll have to decide…

00:37:28.180 --> 00:37:31.210
…on your own, the deeper
meaning of fighting.

00:37:31.210 --> 00:37:32.460
Relena.

00:37:32.460 --> 00:37:34.840
Don’t make me repeat myself.

00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:37.640
I won’t allow such rude
comments.

00:37:43.520 --> 00:37:45.360
We can’t catch that.

00:37:45.940 --> 00:37:48.370
They’re heading toward
the Space Port.

00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:51.450
They seem to be in a rush
for people going to Earth.

00:37:51.450 --> 00:37:53.580
That’s because they’re
gonna escape.

00:37:53.580 --> 00:37:55.150
Escape?

00:37:55.150 --> 00:37:57.540
Then why did they bother
to take over this place?

00:38:00.160 --> 00:38:01.340
Come on!

00:38:01.340 --> 00:38:04.540
Remember, she is Treize’s
daughter after all.

00:38:04.540 --> 00:38:07.680
I’m more concerned about
the man known as Dekim.

00:38:07.680 --> 00:38:09.880
The name Dekim Barton
rings a bell…

00:38:10.290 --> 00:38:12.260
They can’t be serious!

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:14.840
They’re planning to go ahead
with Operation Meteor?

00:38:14.840 --> 00:38:16.260
Yeah.

00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:18.890
But I’ll do everything
I can to stop them.

00:38:24.850 --> 00:38:25.940
<i>Master Quatre.</i>

00:38:25.940 --> 00:38:28.240
<i>We’ll reach the resources
disposal satellite…</i>

00:38:28.240 --> 00:38:29.530
<i>…in twenty seconds.</i>

00:38:29.530 --> 00:38:30.570
All right.

00:38:30.570 --> 00:38:34.570
<i>If it looks too dangerous,
return to the ship at once.</i>

00:38:34.570 --> 00:38:35.740
Yeah.

00:38:36.530 --> 00:38:37.860
It’s here!

00:38:49.830 --> 00:38:52.170
<i>Commencing countdown!</i>

00:38:53.550 --> 00:38:56.270
<i>Seven, six, five…</i>

00:38:56.460 --> 00:38:58.940
four… three… two…

00:38:59.720 --> 00:39:01.350
<i>one… zero!</i>

00:39:14.530 --> 00:39:16.190
Master Quatre!

00:39:22.240 --> 00:39:24.080
<i>I’m… I’m okay.</i>

00:39:24.080 --> 00:39:26.500
<i>I’ve managed to arrive
on the satellite.</i>

00:39:29.830 --> 00:39:31.580
Take care, everyone.

00:39:31.580 --> 00:39:33.470
<i>Say hi to the Goddess
on Venus.</i>

00:39:43.400 --> 00:39:45.230
The air remaining on the ship…

00:39:45.230 --> 00:39:47.850
…has minimized the rise
in temperatures.

00:39:47.850 --> 00:39:51.810
But it’s still hotter than
a desert in here.

00:39:57.110 --> 00:39:58.280
Hi.

00:39:58.650 --> 00:40:00.360
So we meet again.

00:40:08.910 --> 00:40:11.970
The Preventer cruiser has
changed course.

00:40:11.970 --> 00:40:13.800
They’ve realized what’s
happening.

00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:14.970
But it’s too late!

00:40:15.590 --> 00:40:18.310
By the time they arrive at this
natural resources satellite…

00:40:18.310 --> 00:40:20.980
…the ruler of Earth Sphere
will have changed already.

00:40:20.980 --> 00:40:23.100
Send out the Serpent troops,
at once!

00:40:23.100 --> 00:40:24.260
Yes, sir.

00:40:24.260 --> 00:40:25.850
Open the gate on Earth’s side!

00:40:38.150 --> 00:40:40.160
Unidentified mobile suit ahead!

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:41.120
What?!

00:40:41.120 --> 00:40:42.960
Checking the model of
the mobile suit.

00:40:44.610 --> 00:40:46.000
It’s the Tallgeese!

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:47.340
Treize?

00:40:47.340 --> 00:40:48.340
No.

00:40:48.340 --> 00:40:49.750
It must be Zechs.

00:40:49.750 --> 00:40:51.870
The Tallgeese is coming for us!

00:41:17.190 --> 00:41:19.450
My hunch was correct.

00:41:19.450 --> 00:41:21.120
I guess there’s still a place…

00:41:21.120 --> 00:41:23.410
…for a man who can’t
get used to peace.

00:41:23.410 --> 00:41:26.460
The Serpent suits can’t
fight back…

00:41:26.460 --> 00:41:28.250
…wearing their atmosphere
shielding devices!

00:41:28.250 --> 00:41:30.040
Should they remove them?

00:41:30.040 --> 00:41:31.830
No need.

00:41:31.830 --> 00:41:34.170
<i>This is Preventer Wind.</i>

00:41:34.750 --> 00:41:36.620
Zechs Marquise!

00:41:36.620 --> 00:41:38.510
I thought you were dead.

00:41:38.510 --> 00:41:40.170
<i>I was.</i>

00:41:40.170 --> 00:41:43.520
<i>But, I find that I can’t
sleep in my grave…</i>

00:41:43.520 --> 00:41:46.430
<i>…while Treize’s spirit is
still roaming about.</i>

00:41:47.730 --> 00:41:50.640
<i>I heard about you from Quinze…</i>

00:41:50.640 --> 00:41:51.980
<i>…Dekim Barton.</i>

00:41:51.980 --> 00:41:54.600
<i>Surrender and disarm
yourselves at once!</i>

00:41:55.690 --> 00:41:57.900
Shoot us if you dare.

00:41:57.900 --> 00:41:58.870
What?

00:41:58.870 --> 00:42:01.660
If you fire at us,
you’ll quickly realize…

00:42:01.660 --> 00:42:04.200
…that these Serpents aren’t
our last resort.

00:42:04.200 --> 00:42:05.120
<i>Damn you!</i>

00:42:05.120 --> 00:42:07.920
Didn’t Quinze tell you?

00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:11.340
I was the one who created
Operation Meteor.

00:42:12.200 --> 00:42:14.300
X-18999…

00:42:17.250 --> 00:42:18.340
That’s right.

00:42:18.340 --> 00:42:21.970
We can drop that colony
any time we wish.

00:42:21.970 --> 00:42:24.640
If you continue to insist
on interfering…

00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:28.470
…we will drop X-18999
onto Earth!

00:42:29.890 --> 00:42:32.430
Drop your weapons
and surrender!

00:42:32.430 --> 00:42:34.280
Unlike Quinze…

00:42:34.280 --> 00:42:37.740
…I have no intention of
inviting you to be our leader.

00:42:37.740 --> 00:42:41.730
But I’ll consider you as
a soldier under Mariemaia.

00:43:10.430 --> 00:43:12.020
Now, Earth.

00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:15.020
Show me what your
true idea of justice is.

00:43:15.020 --> 00:43:16.640
Drop the colony onto Earth?!

00:43:17.270 --> 00:43:18.820
Stop this at once!

00:43:18.820 --> 00:43:21.030
There’s no reason to do that!

00:43:21.030 --> 00:43:22.240
Relena.

00:43:22.240 --> 00:43:23.940
Please calm down.

00:43:24.360 --> 00:43:25.740
I won’t need to do this.

00:43:25.740 --> 00:43:29.320
So long as all of mankind
bows before me.

00:43:29.320 --> 00:43:32.420
Do you really believe the people
will bow before you?

00:43:32.990 --> 00:43:37.130
Yes, because in your role
as the former Queen Relena…

00:43:37.130 --> 00:43:39.840
…you entrusted me with
the highest position…

00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:41.300
…of the Earth Sphere.

00:43:41.300 --> 00:43:42.550
You must be joking!

00:43:42.550 --> 00:43:44.890
As the Vice Foreign Minister…

00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:46.640
…you’re trusted by the colonies.

00:43:46.640 --> 00:43:49.680
You have a much greater
level of influential power…

00:43:49.680 --> 00:43:52.310
…over the people than
even you realize yourself.

00:43:52.310 --> 00:43:54.360
And that’s why you abducted me.

00:43:54.850 --> 00:43:56.720
Now you’ve got the picture.

00:44:02.690 --> 00:44:05.900
The temperature in here
is above eighty degrees.

00:44:05.900 --> 00:44:08.570
I’ll just think of it
as a big sauna.

00:44:20.750 --> 00:44:22.080
This better work.

00:44:32.890 --> 00:44:34.720
Five… four…

00:44:36.510 --> 00:44:39.680
This angle should take it
straight in Earth’s direction.

00:44:52.450 --> 00:44:55.910
It should get a bit
cooler now.

00:45:04.920 --> 00:45:06.130
Operation Meteor.

00:45:06.960 --> 00:45:10.420
That’s what they called
Gundams’ descent to Earth.

00:45:10.420 --> 00:45:13.630
But it was initially something
completely different.

00:45:13.970 --> 00:45:16.400
The rotation of a colony
is increased…

00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:18.690
…causing its stability in 
the Lagrange Point to fail…{Then the balancing mechanism
is destroyed at La Grange…}

00:45:18.690 --> 00:45:20.430
…hurling the colony
toward Earth.

00:45:20.430 --> 00:45:22.280
As this causes chaos
on Earth…

00:45:22.280 --> 00:45:24.570
…the Gundams are sent
to take over.

00:45:24.570 --> 00:45:27.240
That’s the general outline of
the original Operation Meteor.

00:45:37.740 --> 00:45:39.240
What took you?

00:45:40.280 --> 00:45:41.500
How about that.

00:45:41.500 --> 00:45:44.510
Our objectives ended up
being the same after all.

00:45:44.510 --> 00:45:45.840
Give me a hand.

00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:48.390
They’ve got a complex
lock on the system.

00:45:48.390 --> 00:45:51.720
It’s taking time to re-establish
the colony’s stability control.

00:45:51.720 --> 00:45:52.470
Sure.

00:45:54.970 --> 00:45:56.690
We’d better hurry.

00:45:56.690 --> 00:45:59.650
Looks like they’ve started
sending in troops to Earth.

00:45:59.650 --> 00:46:01.900
I can’t seem to break
the final lock.

00:46:01.900 --> 00:46:04.900
We’ll have to reconnect
the lines directly.

00:46:04.900 --> 00:46:08.070
Many friends that I worked
with are on this colony.

00:46:08.070 --> 00:46:09.490
When I realized Dekim’s plans…

00:46:09.490 --> 00:46:12.200
…were really the original
Operation Meteor…

00:46:12.200 --> 00:46:14.820
…this is the only way I
could think of to stop him.

00:46:14.820 --> 00:46:18.110
But it’s taken me way
too long to get here.

00:46:18.110 --> 00:46:19.670
How about Wufei?

00:46:19.670 --> 00:46:23.620
Did he become Mariemaia’s
soldier just to get their plans?

00:46:23.620 --> 00:46:25.800
No, he hates roundabout
approaches.

00:46:31.460 --> 00:46:33.250
Okay, we’re done.

00:46:33.250 --> 00:46:34.630
This is Duo.

00:46:35.670 --> 00:46:37.480
Are you absolutely sure?!

00:46:37.480 --> 00:46:39.510
You guys stopped
Operation Meteor?!

00:46:43.850 --> 00:46:45.400
<i>This is Wind.</i>

00:46:45.400 --> 00:46:46.740
<i>I’m destroying MO-III!</i>

00:47:02.870 --> 00:47:04.300
You were late!

00:47:04.300 --> 00:47:05.580
See you again!

00:47:11.750 --> 00:47:13.390
We were too late.

00:47:13.390 --> 00:47:14.720
Don’t worry about it.

00:47:14.720 --> 00:47:17.230
At least we were able to
save the colony.

00:47:17.230 --> 00:47:19.390
We have you completely
surrounded.

00:47:19.390 --> 00:47:20.980
Come out with your hands up.

00:47:20.980 --> 00:47:22.510
It’s over.

00:47:22.510 --> 00:47:24.680
Not necessarily.

00:47:24.680 --> 00:47:26.440
I got some mail from Quatre.

00:47:26.970 --> 00:47:28.600
<i>Quatre here.</i>

00:47:28.600 --> 00:47:32.410
<i>I’ve just redirected the resources
disposal satellite toward Earth.</i>

00:47:32.410 --> 00:47:36.150
<i>It should reach the Earth’s orbit
within twenty-four hours.</i>

00:47:36.150 --> 00:47:38.990
Duo, send Quatre a message.

00:47:38.990 --> 00:47:42.990
Tell him to send Wing Zero in
the HES-88 direction.

00:47:42.990 --> 00:47:44.210
You kidding?!

00:47:44.210 --> 00:47:46.250
I’ll pick up Wing Zero in space.

00:47:46.250 --> 00:47:48.010
It’ll save time that way.

00:47:48.660 --> 00:47:49.760
Open the door!

00:47:49.760 --> 00:47:51.170
Open up!

00:47:51.170 --> 00:47:53.970
You can take the shuttle
in the fourth hangar.

00:47:53.970 --> 00:47:57.090
Duo, I have another favor.

00:47:57.090 --> 00:47:58.810
That’s not like you.

00:47:58.810 --> 00:48:01.350
Suddenly asking me
all these favors.

00:48:01.350 --> 00:48:02.600
Hit me!

00:48:02.600 --> 00:48:04.430
Have you gone crazy?!

00:48:04.430 --> 00:48:05.440
Never mind!

00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:06.900
Tear down the door!

00:48:06.900 --> 00:48:08.520
Hurry up!

00:48:08.520 --> 00:48:10.850
Well, you asked for it.

00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:13.110
I’ll give you my best punch!

00:48:17.190 --> 00:48:19.150
Why in the…

00:48:19.150 --> 00:48:20.710
For our own good.

00:48:20.710 --> 00:48:21.910
That’s one for one.

00:48:23.870 --> 00:48:25.170
He’s all yours.

00:48:25.170 --> 00:48:26.330
Right.

00:48:31.540 --> 00:48:32.840
Don’t worry.

00:48:32.840 --> 00:48:34.300
I’ve taken care of them.

00:48:34.300 --> 00:48:37.180
But they prevented the
colony’s instability.

00:48:38.550 --> 00:48:39.630
Stop!

00:48:40.050 --> 00:48:41.230
Freeze! Wait!

00:49:01.820 --> 00:49:03.070
Zechs…

00:49:19.460 --> 00:49:21.130
Is that you, Noin?

00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:24.520
I’ve come to pick you up.

00:49:25.180 --> 00:49:26.430
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:49:28.550 --> 00:49:30.730
<i>Noin, how have you been?</i>

00:49:31.720 --> 00:49:32.850
Good.

00:49:33.680 --> 00:49:36.700
Zechs, it’s been one year
and two days.

00:49:42.150 --> 00:49:45.740
After Colony 196, Christmas.

00:49:46.490 --> 00:49:49.000
Mariemaia’s army has captured
the Presidential Residence…

00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:51.550
…of the Earth Sphere
United Nation.

00:49:51.550 --> 00:49:53.590
As snow continues to fall…

00:49:53.590 --> 00:49:56.680
…peace on Earth has ended
after one short year.

00:49:56.680 --> 00:50:01.760
And the Preventers, currently the
only means of retaliation…

00:50:01.760 --> 00:50:05.180
…were just too powerless
to make a difference.

00:50:05.590 --> 00:50:15.350
<i>As long as we can look each
other in the eye and understand</i>

00:50:15.350 --> 00:50:25.320
<i>People will go on
freely and without hesitation</i>

00:50:25.320 --> 00:50:34.830
<i>When we’ve overcome our mistakes
we can be truly kind</i>

00:50:34.830 --> 00:50:39.330
<i>You and I have discovered</i>

00:50:39.330 --> 00:50:44.600
<i>A great strength that
we know as love</i>

00:50:44.600 --> 00:50:48.930
<i>I believe your love, shivering</i>

00:50:48.930 --> 00:50:53.650
<i>With a kiss I make a silent wish</i>

00:50:53.650 --> 00:50:58.940
<i>Promise me this,
please never forget</i>

00:50:58.940 --> 00:51:03.950
<i>You exist in me, and I in you</i>

00:51:03.950 --> 00:51:08.210
<i>I believe your dreams,
my growing feelings for you</i>

00:51:08.210 --> 00:51:13.130
<i>I change this longing
to prayers for you</i>

00:51:12.870 --> 00:51:13.840
<i>It’s here.</i>

00:51:13.130 --> 00:51:18.000
<i>If only you could hear
this heartbeat of mine</i>

00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:27.920
<i>Beating strong and hard
so far away</i>

00:51:46.110 --> 00:51:53.080
<i>Nothing is gained,
and no one stays</i>

00:51:53.080 --> 00:51:56.590
<i>Let me offer to the baby’s
small hand</i>

00:51:56.590 --> 00:52:00.370
<i>This genuine throbbing
of my heart</i>

00:52:00.370 --> 00:52:07.420
<i>We all want to be held
in the priceless warmth forever</i>

00:52:07.420 --> 00:52:14.650
<i>Like the warmth of the sunlight
as it shines through the forest</i>

00:52:14.650 --> 00:52:17.820
<i>I believe your love,
the will to never give up</i>

00:52:17.820 --> 00:52:21.490
<i>As you spread out those
scarred and battered wings</i>

00:52:21.490 --> 00:52:28.490
<i>You soar through the skies
and portray an endless dream</i>

00:52:50.510 --> 00:52:51.760
Heero.

00:53:13.580 --> 00:53:17.040
Closing Gate 1, closing Gate 2.

00:53:17.040 --> 00:53:18.750
Closing Gates 3 and 4.

00:53:18.750 --> 00:53:20.960
Closing Gates 5 and 6.

00:53:20.960 --> 00:53:23.790
Brussels Presidential Residence
blockade complete!

00:53:26.080 --> 00:53:29.250
My castle is now
completely protected.

00:53:29.250 --> 00:53:31.020
Don’t you find it strange?

00:53:31.020 --> 00:53:33.810
Why should a shelter
such as this…

00:53:33.810 --> 00:53:36.770
…be necessary in a peaceful
world with no weapons?

00:53:37.760 --> 00:53:42.480
History is much like
an endless waltz.

00:53:42.730 --> 00:53:45.490
The three beats of war, peace
and revolution…

00:53:45.490 --> 00:53:47.650
…continue on forever.

00:53:47.650 --> 00:53:52.070
However, history will change
with my coronation.

00:53:52.070 --> 00:53:56.360
The instant the year
After Colony 196 ends…

00:53:56.360 --> 00:53:59.170
…I will be on the top
of the Earth Sphere.

00:53:59.170 --> 00:54:02.250
And a new age will arrive.

00:54:14.230 --> 00:54:16.350
You’re dropping this colony
onto Earth?!

00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:18.900
You’re nuts!

00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:21.920
I’m piloting Nataku to wipe
out the evils of the universe!

00:54:22.220 --> 00:54:26.240
The Alliance has already decided
to dispose of this colony.

00:54:26.240 --> 00:54:28.070
Rather than just watch…

00:54:28.070 --> 00:54:30.570
…it’d be better to go ahead
with Operation Meteor.

00:54:30.570 --> 00:54:33.570
All we need to do is defeat
the necessary enemies!

00:54:37.820 --> 00:54:41.030
I’ll destroy all the evil,
fair and square!

00:54:49.710 --> 00:54:50.880
There he is.

00:55:05.140 --> 00:55:08.100
I won’t let you go to Earth.

00:55:12.310 --> 00:55:14.990
Is this what you interpret
as justice?

00:55:14.990 --> 00:55:17.160
I need to determine myself…

00:55:17.160 --> 00:55:19.920
…whether or not peace at
the expense of people’s lives…

00:55:19.920 --> 00:55:21.700
…can be defined as peace!

00:55:27.450 --> 00:55:30.630
And I will become evil itself
to find out!

00:55:32.420 --> 00:55:34.470
Humanity didn’t change.

00:55:34.470 --> 00:55:38.800
All enemies were defeated,
but Earth didn’t change one bit!

00:56:19.010 --> 00:56:20.010
Huh?

00:56:24.180 --> 00:56:25.470
What’s wrong?

00:56:26.680 --> 00:56:28.520
Hey, what’s this smoke?!

00:56:28.970 --> 00:56:30.350
What is it?

00:56:37.020 --> 00:56:38.490
I’m sorry.

00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:41.700
I need to put you to sleep
just for a bit.

00:56:50.700 --> 00:56:52.960
I can see you’re all okay.

00:57:02.470 --> 00:57:03.890
Well, now.

00:57:03.890 --> 00:57:06.720
Quatre should be here
any time.

00:57:08.260 --> 00:57:09.600
What the?

00:57:23.110 --> 00:57:24.080
Hey!

00:57:24.080 --> 00:57:26.420
You could’ve at least
come to help me!

00:57:26.420 --> 00:57:29.880
There’s nothing wrong with
helping out a friend in need.

00:57:29.880 --> 00:57:32.010
I wasn’t waiting for you.

00:57:32.010 --> 00:57:33.880
But for someone else.

00:57:33.880 --> 00:57:35.220
Sorry to keep you!

00:57:35.220 --> 00:57:37.680
All hostages on this colony
have been rescued!

00:57:38.250 --> 00:57:39.760
Okay, let’s go.

00:57:39.760 --> 00:57:40.510
I see.

00:57:40.510 --> 00:57:42.350
So this is who you meant.

00:57:42.350 --> 00:57:43.850
Thank you, Duo.

00:57:43.850 --> 00:57:46.730
You were kind enough to leave
me plenty of good treats.

00:57:46.730 --> 00:57:49.020
If you’re joking, that’s cruel.

00:57:49.020 --> 00:57:51.270
But if you’re being sarcastic,
that’s even worse!

00:58:14.080 --> 00:58:16.050
The more you fight…

00:58:16.050 --> 00:58:18.430
…the more sacrifices for
peace become a waste.

00:58:18.430 --> 00:58:20.420
You must’ve realized that!

00:58:31.310 --> 00:58:33.360
The war we fought is over!

00:58:33.360 --> 00:58:35.110
So we don’t need warriors?

00:58:35.110 --> 00:58:38.440
Do soldiers who know nothing
but battle get tossed aside?

00:58:40.190 --> 00:58:43.410
Soldiers have fought to
attain a sense of peace!

00:58:43.410 --> 00:58:45.320
Believe in the world we live in!

00:58:48.660 --> 00:58:52.170
I’m acting for the people
who were used as weapons!

00:58:52.170 --> 00:58:55.300
I’m fighting for all soldiers,
including you!

00:58:56.500 --> 00:58:57.510
Wufei.

00:58:57.510 --> 00:59:00.010
You and I are fighting
like this.

00:59:00.010 --> 00:59:03.970
Don’t you feel fulfilled as
I do, when you’re fighting?

00:59:04.550 --> 00:59:06.350
You and I are the same!

00:59:06.350 --> 00:59:10.300
We can only acknowledge our
existence on the battlefield!

00:59:13.940 --> 00:59:16.690
Just remember, Wufei,
Treize is dead!

00:59:16.690 --> 00:59:18.240
You’ve already defeated him!

00:59:18.240 --> 00:59:19.650
You’re wrong!

00:59:19.650 --> 00:59:22.020
I still fight him, even now!

00:59:35.670 --> 00:59:36.800
Zechs.

00:59:36.800 --> 00:59:39.840
The Brussels Presidential
Residence is shielded!

00:59:39.840 --> 00:59:41.260
We can’t get to it!

00:59:41.260 --> 00:59:42.590
I realize that!

00:59:42.590 --> 00:59:46.380
But unless I do what I can,
no one will stand against them!

00:59:50.270 --> 00:59:52.270
<i>Who are you waiting for?</i>

00:59:52.270 --> 00:59:54.400
For those who hope for peace.

00:59:54.400 --> 00:59:57.150
If people allow Mariemaia
to do as she wishes…

00:59:57.150 --> 01:00:00.280
…they’ll create a second
Milliardo Peacecraft.

01:00:16.240 --> 01:00:17.300
<i>Noin.</i>

01:00:17.300 --> 01:00:19.420
<i>You don’t have to stick by me.</i>

01:00:19.420 --> 01:00:20.090
Zechs.

01:00:20.090 --> 01:00:24.250
<i>I told you a year ago that
I’ll never leave your side.</i>

01:00:25.290 --> 01:00:27.420
I’ve waited all this time.

01:00:27.420 --> 01:00:29.840
I don’t want to wait any more.

01:00:30.550 --> 01:00:31.600
Understood.

01:00:46.480 --> 01:00:49.540
I do not consent to
Relena Peacecraft’s ways.

01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:51.710
Her belief that peace comes
from discarding weapons…

01:00:51.710 --> 01:00:54.040
…and confining soldiers
is wrong!

01:00:54.620 --> 01:00:57.000
So that’s why you’re allowing
Mariemaia’s autocracy?!

01:00:57.000 --> 01:01:00.370
That’s where the souls of
soldiers are congregated!

01:01:02.620 --> 01:01:04.430
That may be okay for now.

01:01:04.430 --> 01:01:07.640
But Mariemaia will end up
repeating history!

01:01:07.640 --> 01:01:10.210
A history full of miserable
wars.

01:01:10.210 --> 01:01:12.270
Unless we stop this
process now…

01:01:12.270 --> 01:01:15.390
…more soldiers like ourselves
will become necessary.

01:01:15.390 --> 01:01:16.520
If that happens…

01:01:16.520 --> 01:01:19.860
…a history of tragedy will
keep repeating itself.

01:01:20.560 --> 01:01:22.490
Wufei, tell me.

01:01:22.490 --> 01:01:24.490
How many more people
must we kill?

01:01:29.860 --> 01:01:33.820
How many more times must
I kill that girl and her dog?

01:01:40.620 --> 01:01:43.410
Zero won’t tell me anything.

01:01:43.410 --> 01:01:45.540
<i>Tell me, Wufei!</i>

01:02:13.860 --> 01:02:17.410
Would an event like that
have to be repeated?

01:02:23.040 --> 01:02:25.090
<i>Are you both ready to go?</i>

01:02:25.090 --> 01:02:27.370
Yeah, anytime you are!

01:02:27.370 --> 01:02:30.100
This is what Operation Meteor
should be.

01:02:30.540 --> 01:02:32.170
Let’s go!

01:02:48.940 --> 01:02:52.080
Tallgeese and Taurus are past
our point D number 3 defenses!

01:02:52.080 --> 01:02:54.080
What can they do with
only two suits?!

01:02:54.080 --> 01:02:56.620
Send our remaining assault
troops to point D.

01:02:56.620 --> 01:02:57.460
Yes, sir!

01:02:58.070 --> 01:03:02.580
Looks like a sibling reunion
will be difficult this time.

01:03:04.580 --> 01:03:06.510
<i>We are facing fools…</i>

01:03:06.510 --> 01:03:08.970
<i>…that are hopelessly rebelling
against the new order.</i>

01:03:09.880 --> 01:03:15.270
<i>Consider the significance of
the lives that will be lost.</i>

01:03:15.270 --> 01:03:16.390
Grandpa.

01:03:16.390 --> 01:03:18.730
I thought there wouldn’t
be any more wars.

01:03:18.730 --> 01:03:20.050
That’s right.

01:03:21.430 --> 01:03:25.060
Then, why are those people
still having a war?

01:03:25.060 --> 01:03:26.280
Unfortunately…

01:03:26.280 --> 01:03:30.270
…not everyone in the world
is as sensible as you.

01:03:32.310 --> 01:03:35.570
But in fact people
are too sensible.

01:03:35.570 --> 01:03:38.830
Too few people are
retaliating against Mariemaia.

01:03:42.160 --> 01:03:44.660
Does she believe this
is Treize’s ideal?

01:03:45.550 --> 01:03:49.260
She doesn’t realize she’s
merely Dekim’s puppet.

01:04:34.790 --> 01:04:36.350
This is it.

01:04:36.350 --> 01:04:38.720
I’m not saying any
good-byes yet, Zechs!

01:04:38.720 --> 01:04:40.380
Of course not!

01:04:47.810 --> 01:04:50.060
I’m glad we weren’t too late.

01:04:50.770 --> 01:04:51.940
Quatre?!

01:04:58.230 --> 01:05:00.490
You two are truly impressive.

01:05:00.490 --> 01:05:03.460
You’ve fought this many
without killing one soldier.

01:05:03.460 --> 01:05:06.790
I’d be glad if we could teach
these people something.

01:05:18.090 --> 01:05:22.300
Let’s take the weapons
and war itself with us to hell!

01:05:38.820 --> 01:05:40.580
About two hundred fifty left.

01:05:40.580 --> 01:05:42.580
That’s fifty suits each.

01:05:42.580 --> 01:05:45.170
If that’s all, then we should
be able to manage.

01:05:50.130 --> 01:05:51.580
Gundams?!

01:05:53.620 --> 01:05:57.290
How much longer will those
punks retaliate against me?!

01:05:57.790 --> 01:06:00.100
Even if they did destroy
the mobile suits…

01:06:00.100 --> 01:06:03.260
…there’s no way they can
break into this shelter.

01:06:03.260 --> 01:06:05.800
What they’re doing
is meaningless.

01:06:08.800 --> 01:06:10.310
I’ve been…

01:06:10.310 --> 01:06:11.860
What’s wrong, Relena?

01:06:15.730 --> 01:06:17.230
I’ve been…

01:06:20.110 --> 01:06:22.610
I’ve been running from
the truth!

01:06:26.240 --> 01:06:27.290
<i>People!</i>

01:06:27.290 --> 01:06:29.790
<i>Do not fear the broadcast
you’re watching!</i>

01:06:30.950 --> 01:06:33.960
<i>Peace is not something
that is handed to you.</i>

01:06:33.960 --> 01:06:35.250
<i>Each person must…</i>

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:37.470
Hey, wasn’t that!

01:06:37.470 --> 01:06:39.340
That was Queen Relena!

01:06:40.290 --> 01:06:43.390
It’s still much too early for
your appearance to the people…

01:06:43.390 --> 01:06:44.430
…Former Queen.

01:06:46.420 --> 01:06:49.680
Are you guiding the public
to battle?

01:06:49.680 --> 01:06:53.110
Doesn’t that go against your
Total Peace Policies?!

01:06:53.640 --> 01:06:56.150
I am no longer a Peacecraft.

01:06:56.150 --> 01:07:00.240
What’s needed now is not
a principle or an assertion.

01:07:00.240 --> 01:07:01.780
But the heart to hope for peace.

01:07:10.990 --> 01:07:13.750
Are you people just going
keep sitting on your butts?

01:07:13.750 --> 01:07:14.500
What?

01:07:14.500 --> 01:07:18.680
Mariemaia is the master you
have all been waiting for.

01:07:19.330 --> 01:07:21.930
Come on, wag your tails
and run to her.

01:07:22.170 --> 01:07:22.970
Hey!

01:07:22.970 --> 01:07:25.310
Are you comparing us
to dogs?!

01:07:25.310 --> 01:07:27.230
Oh, I beg your pardon.

01:07:27.230 --> 01:07:28.850
Let me correct myself.

01:07:28.850 --> 01:07:32.860
You’re not dogs that wag their
tail in front of their master.

01:07:32.860 --> 01:07:34.820
You’re the tail that is wagged!

01:07:35.060 --> 01:07:36.940
Shut your mouth, lady!

01:07:36.940 --> 01:07:38.320
You’re looking at a man…

01:07:38.320 --> 01:07:41.450
…who shot down five mobile
suits in the war a year ago!

01:07:41.450 --> 01:07:42.320
That’s funny.

01:07:42.320 --> 01:07:45.110
I see no men around here.

01:07:45.110 --> 01:07:48.660
The only men I know
are either buried…

01:07:48.660 --> 01:07:51.040
…or are broadcast on that screen!

01:08:42.120 --> 01:08:45.720
Peace is not something
that is just handed to us…

01:08:51.380 --> 01:08:54.100
I think we might have
been mistaken.

01:08:54.100 --> 01:08:55.390
You’re right.

01:08:55.390 --> 01:08:57.520
We should be the ones fighting.

01:08:57.520 --> 01:08:59.940
Of course, we won’t use
any weapons to fight.

01:09:00.430 --> 01:09:03.400
Is that the responsibility
given to us survivors?

01:09:04.270 --> 01:09:06.700
We must prove that we
deserve this peace…

01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:10.580
…that we have worked so
hard to obtain.

01:09:10.580 --> 01:09:14.160
We must confirm that we
are worthy of this freedom.

01:09:14.950 --> 01:09:16.830
Okay, I’m going!

01:09:16.830 --> 01:09:19.590
I’m going to the Presidential
Palace—to Relena!

01:09:19.590 --> 01:09:20.760
You mean now?

01:09:20.760 --> 01:09:21.550
Yeah!

01:09:21.550 --> 01:09:22.420
But how?

01:09:22.420 --> 01:09:23.630
We’ll find a way!

01:09:23.630 --> 01:09:24.880
I’m going too!

01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:27.760
I can’t just wait around
and not do anything!

01:09:27.760 --> 01:09:29.100
Count me in, too!

01:09:29.100 --> 01:09:31.140
Anyone else, just follow us!

01:09:31.140 --> 01:09:32.850
Right, I’m joining you!

01:09:32.850 --> 01:09:34.140
I’m going too!

01:09:34.140 --> 01:09:35.310
Me too!

01:09:35.310 --> 01:09:37.020
It’s time that we stood up
for something!

01:09:37.020 --> 01:09:38.610
Will we get there in time?!

01:09:38.610 --> 01:09:40.890
I guess I’ve got no choice.

01:09:41.310 --> 01:09:45.230
Let me give you all
a ride in my vehicle.

01:10:39.530 --> 01:10:40.830
Take this!

01:10:57.550 --> 01:10:58.520
Damn!

01:10:58.520 --> 01:11:01.060
They just keep coming,
all at once!

01:11:05.480 --> 01:11:06.850
Here I go!!

01:11:23.160 --> 01:11:26.510
Looks like we’re fighting
another losing battle.

01:12:08.040 --> 01:12:09.290
Zero.

01:12:09.290 --> 01:12:10.510
Can you move?

01:12:23.260 --> 01:12:24.430
Sure.

01:12:24.800 --> 01:12:26.720
This’ll be your final fight.

01:12:56.130 --> 01:12:57.920
Gundam pilots…

01:12:57.920 --> 01:12:58.970
…that’s enough!

01:12:58.970 --> 01:13:00.390
Leave us and retreat.

01:13:00.390 --> 01:13:01.560
Retreat?!

01:13:05.510 --> 01:13:08.980
If we were fighting to kill,
we’d be done long ago.

01:13:08.980 --> 01:13:12.020
But then coming back here
would be meaningless!

01:13:13.640 --> 01:13:16.020
At this rate, you’d die in vain!

01:13:18.690 --> 01:13:22.120
If we’d planned on retreating,
we would’ve been gone.

01:13:22.120 --> 01:13:25.030
I know it’ll be tough
to keep fighting, though.

01:13:31.790 --> 01:13:34.220
We used to be just like them.

01:13:34.220 --> 01:13:36.590
Dekim coaxed them into
believing…

01:13:36.590 --> 01:13:38.510
…their reason for living
is to fight.

01:13:38.510 --> 01:13:39.060
<i>But…</i>

01:13:39.310 --> 01:13:41.720
Hey, don’t worry about it.

01:13:41.720 --> 01:13:44.800
We’ve gotten pretty good at
these losing battles!

01:13:51.180 --> 01:13:55.440
That’s why we could always
be true to ourselves.

01:13:55.440 --> 01:13:57.700
I didn’t go back to
being a Darlian…

01:13:57.700 --> 01:13:59.940
…to get revenge for my father.

01:13:59.940 --> 01:14:02.120
Nothing can be achieved
through revenge.

01:14:02.120 --> 01:14:05.280
Hatred will only result in
breeding more hatred!

01:14:05.280 --> 01:14:08.710
You only think that way
because you lost your battle.

01:14:08.710 --> 01:14:10.550
But I’m different.

01:14:10.550 --> 01:14:12.830
I will truly be victorious.

01:14:15.010 --> 01:14:16.040
Told you.

01:14:19.130 --> 01:14:21.590
I’ve got nothing left.

01:14:21.590 --> 01:14:24.600
Self-detonating could take out
about half the suits left.

01:14:24.600 --> 01:14:25.940
What do you think?

01:14:25.940 --> 01:14:26.690
No.

01:14:26.690 --> 01:14:29.220
Detonation should be done
away from them.

01:14:29.220 --> 01:14:30.980
Limit the casualties to
just ourselves.

01:14:31.230 --> 01:14:32.570
Guess you’re right.

01:14:37.400 --> 01:14:38.110
What?!

01:14:38.110 --> 01:14:39.270
Above us!

01:14:42.570 --> 01:14:43.530
Wing Zero!

01:14:49.240 --> 01:14:50.880
Locked onto target!

01:14:51.080 --> 01:14:53.830
Another Gundam confirmed!

01:14:53.830 --> 01:14:54.840
What?!

01:14:54.840 --> 01:14:55.800
Mr. Dekim!

01:14:55.800 --> 01:14:58.130
We’re online with one of
the Gundam pilots!

01:14:58.130 --> 01:14:59.330
Heero!

01:14:59.330 --> 01:15:00.760
<i>Let me confirm.</i>

01:15:00.760 --> 01:15:02.970
<i>Your shelter shield’s activated?</i>

01:15:02.970 --> 01:15:04.470
What are you planning?!

01:15:04.470 --> 01:15:06.350
<i>Your shelter is secure?</i>

01:15:06.350 --> 01:15:07.770
Of course it is.

01:15:07.770 --> 01:15:10.020
Admit to yourselves just
how powerless you are!

01:15:10.600 --> 01:15:11.430
<i>Roger.</i>

01:15:22.230 --> 01:15:24.160
Gather all the Serpents here!

01:15:24.160 --> 01:15:25.990
Shoot down Wing Zero!

01:15:26.650 --> 01:15:28.290
What a miserable person.

01:15:28.290 --> 01:15:31.170
He’s not going to prove
anything.

01:15:31.170 --> 01:15:32.960
Are you afraid, Mariemaia?

01:15:43.290 --> 01:15:44.720
That’s impossible!

01:15:44.720 --> 01:15:46.890
How could this be happening?!

01:15:46.890 --> 01:15:48.850
The shield’s lost half
its strength!

01:15:48.850 --> 01:15:52.190
Wing Zero’s aim is accurate
to one hundredth of a unit!

01:15:52.190 --> 01:15:56.680
This shelter will collapse if it’s
hit again in the same place!

01:15:56.680 --> 01:15:58.030
Stop it!

01:15:58.030 --> 01:16:00.320
Relena Peacecraft is in here!

01:16:04.230 --> 01:16:05.400
Heero…

01:16:30.480 --> 01:16:31.510
Heero!

01:16:57.740 --> 01:16:59.090
Are you okay?

01:16:59.090 --> 01:17:00.130
Who are you?

01:17:00.130 --> 01:17:02.590
Even though you may
be mistaken…

01:17:02.590 --> 01:17:05.760
…I can’t allow the daughter of
His Excellency, Treize, to die.

01:17:08.460 --> 01:17:09.720
Mr. Dekim!

01:17:09.720 --> 01:17:12.940
Another Gundam has arrived at
defense line number 4 point E!

01:17:12.940 --> 01:17:13.690
Also…

01:17:15.680 --> 01:17:18.260
There is no way we’d obey you!

01:17:18.260 --> 01:17:20.350
We don’t want any more wars!

01:17:22.400 --> 01:17:25.770
We want to protect the peace
here ourselves!

01:17:28.190 --> 01:17:31.610
Battles like these are not
decided by the soldiers.

01:17:32.410 --> 01:17:35.780
Thanks to them,
I can give up fighting!

01:17:36.410 --> 01:17:38.590
This is goodbye, Treize.

01:17:40.200 --> 01:17:41.550
Zechs.

01:17:42.870 --> 01:17:44.300
This is good.

01:17:44.300 --> 01:17:46.760
We don’t have to abandon
hope just yet.

01:17:47.460 --> 01:17:49.720
The detonating device missed
its chance again.

01:17:50.210 --> 01:17:51.970
Who the hell are they?!

01:17:51.970 --> 01:17:54.770
While His Excellency fought
losing battles…

01:17:54.770 --> 01:17:57.980
…he truly loved people
who weren’t afraid to fight.

01:17:57.980 --> 01:18:01.150
And that’s why people can
accept the Gundams.

01:18:01.890 --> 01:18:05.480
It is not the victor that moves
the heart of the people.

01:18:14.900 --> 01:18:15.870
This is crazy!

01:18:15.870 --> 01:18:18.000
We cannot be defeated!

01:18:18.000 --> 01:18:19.670
We, the Barton family…

01:18:19.670 --> 01:18:22.450
…are the true rulers
of the Earth Sphere!

01:18:22.450 --> 01:18:24.160
Miss Mariemaia!

01:18:24.160 --> 01:18:26.880
Assume your position
as head of the Earth Sphere!

01:18:27.830 --> 01:18:30.170
I am… victorious…

01:18:34.050 --> 01:18:37.060
I’m carrying out my
father’s desires…

01:18:41.140 --> 01:18:42.350
Forgive me!

01:18:46.190 --> 01:18:47.410
Excuse me.

01:18:47.410 --> 01:18:50.070
But it’s time you opened
your eyes, Mariemaia.

01:18:51.440 --> 01:18:54.040
Relena…

01:18:54.400 --> 01:18:57.250
You have learned what
real fear is.

01:18:57.250 --> 01:19:02.160
So I’m sure you can see
all the mistakes you’ve made.

01:19:02.960 --> 01:19:04.960
Stop right there,
Relena Peacecraft.

01:19:05.710 --> 01:19:09.750
I can’t allow you to brainwash
my Mariemaia with such trash!

01:19:09.750 --> 01:19:12.380
If you wish to shoot me,
go right ahead!

01:19:12.380 --> 01:19:13.930
I’m prepared to die!

01:19:14.670 --> 01:19:17.310
Then I’ll tell you the truth
before you die!

01:19:17.310 --> 01:19:20.180
The public must obey the victor!

01:19:26.930 --> 01:19:28.150
Mariemaia!

01:19:31.560 --> 01:19:34.870
We can always create a
replacement for Mariemaia!

01:19:34.870 --> 01:19:36.750
I made her after all!

01:19:36.750 --> 01:19:37.570
Dekim!

01:19:48.160 --> 01:19:50.220
I’ve executed the rebel.

01:19:50.220 --> 01:19:54.300
I express my apologies for
betraying His Excellency, Treize.

01:20:00.550 --> 01:20:02.850
Mariemaia, hold on!

01:20:03.800 --> 01:20:06.770
Relena, I was mistaken.

01:20:06.770 --> 01:20:08.650
I’m sorry.

01:20:09.140 --> 01:20:10.280
Mariemaia.

01:20:10.280 --> 01:20:12.240
I’ll put you of your misery.

01:20:12.860 --> 01:20:14.020
Heero.

01:20:19.570 --> 01:20:20.870
Thank you.

01:20:29.750 --> 01:20:31.830
I’ve killed Mariemaia.

01:20:34.210 --> 01:20:36.300
I… I…

01:20:36.750 --> 01:20:38.550
I will never kill again.

01:20:40.590 --> 01:20:42.340
I don’t have to kill any more.

01:20:44.800 --> 01:20:45.860
Heero!

01:20:52.440 --> 01:20:53.610
Heero…

01:20:55.690 --> 01:20:57.240
There’s still hope for her!

01:20:57.240 --> 01:20:58.220
Take her to the doctor!

01:20:58.220 --> 01:20:58.790
Yes, Ma’am!

01:20:59.650 --> 01:21:02.450
Finally it’s over.

01:22:04.050 --> 01:22:07.100
This time it’s good-bye
for real, buddy.

01:22:18.110 --> 01:22:20.690
I’ve become nameless again.

01:22:20.690 --> 01:22:22.410
Trowa sounds fine to me.

01:22:22.410 --> 01:22:24.160
Why not keep it, Trowa?

01:22:24.820 --> 01:22:27.000
Names are given to you
by others.

01:22:27.000 --> 01:22:29.540
No point wasting time
worrying about it.

01:22:29.540 --> 01:22:33.410
What’s important is having
a place we can call home.

01:22:33.410 --> 01:22:35.580
Yeah, you’re right.

01:22:53.810 --> 01:22:56.980
Nataku, may you rest in peace.

01:22:58.900 --> 01:23:01.660
Noin and Zechs have
disappeared somewhere.

01:23:01.660 --> 01:23:05.240
What do you say?
Wanna come work with me?

01:23:05.780 --> 01:23:07.570
As a Preventer?

01:23:09.660 --> 01:23:11.030
Why not?

01:23:15.500 --> 01:23:17.130
Are you sure?

01:23:17.130 --> 01:23:20.420
The Terra Formation Project
hasn’t officially started yet.

01:23:20.420 --> 01:23:24.470
Relena is working on it,
and it won’t be easy.

01:23:24.470 --> 01:23:27.810
That’s why a dead person
would be perfect for the job.

01:23:27.810 --> 01:23:29.560
Noin, are you sure you…

01:23:29.560 --> 01:23:33.310
Don’t make me repeat
myself, Zechs.

01:23:39.020 --> 01:23:41.730
After Colony 197.

01:23:41.730 --> 01:23:44.570
Peace has returned
to the people.

01:23:44.570 --> 01:23:47.320
And from this point on…

01:23:47.650 --> 01:23:53.500
…weapons known as mobile suits, 
including the Gundams…

01:23:53.500 --> 01:23:55.910
…were never seen again.

01:24:08.350 --> 01:24:17.990
<i>As long as we can look each
other in the eye and understand</i>

01:24:17.990 --> 01:24:27.960
<i>People will go on
freely and without hesitation</i>

01:24:28.000 --> 01:24:37.320
<i>When we’ve overcome our mistakes
we can be truly kind</i>

01:24:37.340 --> 01:24:41.960
<i>You and I have discovered</i>

01:24:41.960 --> 01:24:47.140
<i>A great strength that
we know as love</i>

01:24:47.140 --> 01:24:51.550
<i>I believe your love, shivering</i>

01:24:51.550 --> 01:24:56.230
<i>With a kiss I make a silent wish</i>

01:24:56.230 --> 01:25:01.440
<i>Promise me this,
please never forget</i>

01:25:01.440 --> 01:25:06.200
<i>You exist in me, and I in you</i>

01:25:06.240 --> 01:25:10.750
<i>I believe your dreams,
my growing feelings for you</i>

01:25:10.750 --> 01:25:15.500
<i>I change this longing
to prayers for you</i>

01:25:15.500 --> 01:25:20.420
<i>If only you could hear
this heartbeat of mine</i>

01:25:20.420 --> 01:25:30.760
<i>Beating strong and hard
so far away</i>

01:25:27.510 --> 01:25:28.430
Mission Complete

01:25:55.860 --> 01:26:02.800
<i>Nothing is gained,
and no one stays</i>

01:26:02.800 --> 01:26:06.390
<i>Let me offer to the baby’s
small hand</i>

01:26:06.390 --> 01:26:10.050
<i>This genuine throbbing
of my heart</i>

01:26:10.050 --> 01:26:17.260
<i>We all want to be held
in the priceless warmth forever</i>

01:26:17.260 --> 01:26:24.360
<i>Like the warmth of the sunlight
as it shines through the forest</i>

01:26:24.360 --> 01:29:39.970
<i>m 401 458 l 1017 458 1017 634 401 634</i>

01:26:24.360 --> 01:26:27.610
<i>I believe your love,
the will to never give up</i>

01:26:27.610 --> 01:26:31.370
<i>As you spread out those
scarred and battered wings</i>

01:26:31.370 --> 01:26:38.420
<i>You soar through the skies
and portray an endless dream</i>

01:26:38.420 --> 01:26:41.460
<i>I believe your dreams,
please show me a smile</i>

01:26:41.460 --> 01:26:45.460
<i>Even in times of unbearable pain</i>

01:26:45.460 --> 01:26:49.090
<i>So that someday we can be proud</i>

01:26:49.090 --> 01:26:56.590
<i>And boast of our precious world
